## Reports staging adapter

runtime/reports/start-staging.sh adapts startup and migration commands from
the upstream Bahmni Reports image, pinned to digest
sha256:3af8e248ae7603126fecb1efacb583e8b6b2bd4e9df0254fc198e8e4a2d63877.
That directory is licensed under AGPL 3.0, included in runtime/reports/LICENSE,
not the MPL license applying to the frontend. The adapter retains the bundled
upstream migrations and application. Its changes remove password-bearing
shell tracing, restrict generated configuration permissions, override the
private configuration URL and start without a debugger. MainReportController.java
is derived from Bahmni/bahmni-reports 1.1.0, revision
8f9d4bbdfec3aacba680a60d7fe47584eb679559. Its changes enforce authenticated
report ownership and per-report privileges, fail closed on verification errors,
stop denied direct generation and prevent duplicate download extensions.
TemplateUploadController.java is derived from the same revision. Its changes
validate XLS content and safe filenames, preserve original workbook bytes,
confine unique file writes to the configured directory, clean partial writes
and return UTF-8 upload acknowledgements. The native check harnesses and
controllers are also AGPL 3.0. No upstream notices or licenses in the original
image are removed.

JasperResponseConverter.java derives from the same Reports revision under
AGPL 3.0. Its native generation/template code is retained; Qorlia supplies the
correct XLS MIME type. MainReportController carries native file content types
explicitly and preserves the JSON queue contract. ReportsExporterCheck.java,
the dependency fetch/install scripts and compatibility manifest are AGPL 3.0.
The manifest pins a Java 11 staging candidate using DynamicReports 6.12.1,
JasperReports 6.21.5, Apache POI 5.4.1 and matching dependencies. Downloaded JARs
retain their own upstream licenses/notices and are not committed here. Original
libraries remain recoverable; this compatibility check is not a completed
production dependency or legal audit.
